  {
    "slug": "cosmere-reading-order",
    "title": "The Cosmere — Reading Order",
    "summary": "A spoiler-conscious path through Sanderson's connected universe — Mistborn eras, Stormlight, the standalones, and where the trap novellas actually belong.",
    "intro": "Sanderson says there's no single mandatory Cosmere order — several books work as entry points. This is the spoiler-conscious path: Mistborn Era 1 first, Secret History only after The Bands of Mourning (his own rule — it torpedoes Era 1 otherwise), Warbreaker before Words of Radiance for a quiet payoff, and The Sunlit Man last. Notes flag the slots that are genuinely flexible. (The Frugal Wizard's Handbook isn't Cosmere, so it isn't here.)",
